        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(line): preserve media polling when body cleanup fails",
        "body": "<details>\n<summary>Additional instructions</summary>\n\nAllow edits from maintainers is enabled for this PR.\n\n</details>\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where LINE inbound media polling could stop on a response-body cleanup error instead of retrying HTTP 202, or could replace the actionable HTTP status for a non-202 failure.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nDiscarded response bodies are still canceled and awaited, but cancellation rejection no longer changes the polling or HTTP-error result. Risk: polling count and backoff must remain unchanged; the regression and runtime proof preserve the request sequence and final status.\n\n## User Impact\n\nLINE media that is still preparing can continue polling, and failed downloads retain the useful LINE HTTP status.\n\n## Evidence\n\nNode v24.18.0 production-entry proof called downloadLineMedia() with native Response/ReadableStream objects and only replaced the network transport seam. The first response was HTTP 202 and both discarded bodies rejected cancellation.\n\nBefore on ec998a0f3fc:\n\n    {\"outcome\":\"rejected\",\"error\":\"cancel failed\",\"fetchCalls\":1,\"cancelCalls\":1}\n\nAfter on current upstream main plus this commit:\n\n    {\"outcome\":\"rejected\",\"error\":\"LINE media download failed for message live-proof (HTTP 404)\",\"fetchCalls\":2,\"cancelCalls\":2}\n\nFocused regression:\n\n    node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/line/src/download.test.ts\n    Test Files  1 passed (1)\n    Tests  10 passed (10)\n\nThe same tests failed before the production change: the 202 path stopped at cancel failed, and the 404 assertion received cancel failed instead of HTTP 404. Targeted oxfmt, direct oxlint, and git diff --check passed. The changed-check wrapper was blocked before reaching these files by current checkout plugin-SDK boundary DTS errors in packages/net-policy/src/ip.ts; full build/check/test are left to fork CI.\n\nAI-assisted: Codex helped implement and review the change; the behavior proof was run manually.\n",
